  "final_message": "The weather app is built, but I couldn't build the Docker image because Docker isn't installed in this sandbox.\n\nWhat I did check:\n- **API:** I ran it through Flask's test client. Registration, login, report create/replace/delete and validation errors all worked, as did the case-insensitive city lookup and recording of lookups. Paging was checked only with `page_size=2`.\n- **Frontend:** `npm run build` (type-check plus Vite) succeeds. I didn't open the UI in a browser.\n\nChoices I made that the spec left open:\n- **Sessions:** login tokens expire after 7 days.\n- **Password rules:** passwords must be at least 8 characters.\n- **Duplicate names:** a duplicate username or city returns 409.\n- **Extra routes:** I added `GET /api/auth/me`, which the frontend uses to show the signed-in username.\n- **Sample data:** it seeds 7 cities on first start.\n- **Database location:** it lives at `data/weather.db`, and a `DATA_DIR` environment variable can override that.\n\nI also added a `.gitignore`.",
